From 7c6b9275014ec1e7975d4911d5a53d4620e172d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Castro <daniel.castro@tecnico.ulisboa.pt>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 23:02:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] power: POWER8 HTM checkpoint, TEXASR/TFIAR int regs, TM
 instruction classes

- htm.hh/htm.cc: HTMCheckpoint with save/restore of all arch state.
  restore() rolls back GPRs/FPRs/CR/XER/LR/CTR/TAR/FPSCR, clears
  MSR[ts] (non-transactional), drops the reservation, sets CR0[EQ]=1
  so the software `tbegin.; beq abort_handler` fallback is taken,
  writes TEXASR failure cause + TFIAR, and redirects PC to the TFHAR
  fallback (tbegin+4). CR0 polarity verified against the Linux kernel
  TM docs and LLVM's HTM builtins (EQ=0 started / EQ=1 failed).
- regs/int.hh: register TEXASR and TFIAR as architectural int regs
  (int_reg::Texasr, int_reg::Tfiar) used to surface abort status.
- insts/tm.hh: HtmMemInst base + TBegin/TEnd/TAbort (HTM mem mgmt)
  and TCheck/TSr (memory-free execute) classes with decoder fields.

Part of the 8-patch POWER8 HTM plan (docs/power8-htm-patches.md).
